Concurrency:
	Concurrency means dealing with multiple tasks during overlapping periods of time.
	
Parallelism
	Multiple tasks literally execute at the same time, usually on different CPU cores.
	
Process
	A process is a running program with its own execution environment and resources.
	
Thread
	A thread is an execution path inside a process.
	Threads are sometimes called lightweight processes. Both processes and threads provide
	 an execution environment, but creating a new thread requires fewer resources than 
	 creating a new process
	 
	 A Thread object represents a thread of execution.